<title>JAPAN: JT says US partner to seek FDA's HIV drug approval.</title>
<headline>JT says US partner to seek FDA's HIV drug approval.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Tobacco Inc said on Thursday that its partner Agouron Pharmaceuticals Inc of the United States would apply for approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to start marketing their jointly developed drug for treating HIV, the virus that causes AIDS.  </p>
<p>Japan Tobacco and Agouron, which was established in 1984, have been collaborating in the development of the drug, VIRACEPT, since December 1994.</p>
<p>The drug has been going through three-stage clinical trials since February, involving more than 700 subjects, Agouron said in a statement.</p>
<p>The application should be submitted to the FDA no later than in the first quarter of 1997, the statement said.</p>
</text>
